04/08/2026

o Systems studied across this tree: PP_3H / pph3 (tri-protonated pyrophosphate,
  H3P2O7(-), in its alpha and beta isomers), PP_4H / pph4 (fully protonated,
  H4P2O7), and 2Mg(2+)[P2O7](4-) / ppimg2 (the bimagnesium complex). The wider
  LFER comparison in 'LFER/LFER_3_mg2/ts_energies.txt' also carries P2O7,
  MgP2O7, H2P2O7 and H4P2O7.

o 'JOBS/'           raw SLURM scratch directories, 'JOB-<id>/', around two
                     thousand of them, auto-generated by the submission tooling
                     across every pipeline in this tree. Arbitrary job ids, not a
                     replica set, not documented individually.
  'cp2k_MD/'        reference CP2K DFT-MD on the PPiMg2 system, predating the NNP
                     work -- see its README.
  'pph3/'           ArcaNN CP2K labeling batch for the pph3 training set.
                     Unrelated to the free-energy study of the same name under
                     'LFER/LFER_3_mg2/pph3/' -- see its README.
  'LFER/'           the downstream free-energy study: pph4, pph3 alpha/beta,
                     ppimg2, plus the committee check in 'NNP_LFER_choice/'.
  'Train_PPiMg2/'   the main ArcaNN training area for ppimg2 ('Simulations/',
                     'initial_dataset/') and the live copy of the LFER study.
  'templates/'      ArcaNN workflow scaffolding, currently just
                     '01_initial_trainingset/'.
  'softwares/'      a live git checkout of the ArcaNN tool itself
                     (github.com/arcann-chem/arcann_training) plus its offline
                     conda bundle. It has its own upstream 'README.md' and I have
                     not added one inside it, to keep untracked files out of a git
                     working tree that is not this project's own data.
  'script/'         flat collection of standalone utility scripts.
  'user_files_MN5/' ArcaNN machine and job-script configuration for MN5.
  'RESULTS/'        pH speciation and the effective-barrier model built on it.

01/10/2026

o Spelled out the direction of the duplicated LFER tree, which the previous
  version of this file left unstated. It is:

      SOURCE  Train_PPiMg2/LFER_3_mg2/   <-- the live, working copy
      MIRROR  LFER/LFER_3_mg2/           <-- the rsync destination

  'LFER/copy_LFER_3_mg2.sh' is a batch job that runs 'rsync -avh' from the first
  to the second, and 'LFER/verify_LFER_3_mg2.sh' re-checks it with '-avhnc', a
  checksum dry run that cannot modify either side. The last verification, logged
  in 'LFER/verify_LFER_3_mg2.log', finished on 28/08/2026 with nothing to
  transfer, so the two trees were byte-identical at that moment across 948 GB.
  The source has been touched since, so they are no longer guaranteed equal.
  Work in 'Train_PPiMg2/LFER_3_mg2/'; treat 'LFER/LFER_3_mg2/' as a backup.
  The same source/mirror pairing applies to 'NNP_LFER_choice/'.

o A consequence of that, and the thing most likely to waste someone's time: the
  detailed per-folder READMEs for the LFER study were written into the MIRROR,
  not into the source. 'LFER/LFER_3_mg2/' carries 82 of them against 29 in
  'Train_PPiMg2/LFER_3_mg2/', so 53 folders are documented on the mirror side
  only. If you are working in the live tree and find a folder undocumented, the
  description almost certainly exists at the same relative path under
  'LFER/LFER_3_mg2/'. Because the rsync runs source-to-destination and carries
  no '--delete', the next sync will not remove them, but adding '--delete'
  would. Worth consolidating.

o Because the two trees are structurally identical, the per-folder documentation
  is not duplicated. Only the mirror copy is described in detail. Within it, the
  three systems sit in parallel directories of the same shape:

      pph4    LFER/LFER_3_mg2/pph4/     H4P2O7, fully protonated
      pph3    LFER/LFER_3_mg2/pph3/     H3P2O7(-), alpha and beta isomers
      ppimg2  LFER/LFER_3_mg2/ppimg2/   2Mg(2+)[P2O7](4-)

  and each follows the same OPES -> SMD -> umbrella sampling -> WHAM chain. See
  'LFER/LFER_3_mg2/README' and the per-system READMEs below it.

o 'Train_PPiMg2/initial_dataset/' now has a 'README.md' describing the folder
  layout and the two extraction generations. The author's own 'README.txt' and
  'new_rep/README' in there were left untouched; they remain the authority on the
  per-replica configuration counts.

o A machine-written structural overview of the whole tree, with absolute paths and
  a per-folder review, is in 'STRUCTURE_OVERVIEW.md' next to this file.

02/10/2026

o MERGED the two copies of the LFER study into one. 'LFER/LFER_3_mg2/' is now the
  single location; 'Train_PPiMg2/LFER_3_mg2/' as a real directory is gone. This
  supersedes the two entries above about source and mirror -- read them as history.

o The merge was not one-directional, because both copies had been worked on after
  the 28/08 sync and each held work the other did not:

    - 114106 files were already byte-identical and needed nothing.
    - 74 files existed only on the LFER side: the 53 per-folder READMEs, the
      'pph3-included' pph4 FES re-run of 02/09 (13 files), 'TS_levels_per_system.py'
      and the four 'ts_levels_*.png' of 24/08.
    - 7 files existed only on the Train side: three '.bak_*' snapshots,
      'ts_energies.txt.bak_20260917', 'ts_levels_v3.png', 'ts_levels_v3_smallerr.png'
      and a '__pycache__' entry.
    - 23 files existed on both with different content.

o How the 23 were resolved, after reading every diff. Nothing was discarded: in each
  case the version that did not win is kept beside the winner, renamed
  '<name>.from_lfer_<date>' or '<name>.from_train_<date>'.

    - 16 of them were the eight 'average_PMF.py' plus the eight 'average_pmf.png'
      they render. The only code difference was the annotation offset,
      'plt.text(x_pos - 0.15, ...)' against '(x_pos + 0.025, ...)'. Same free-energy
      data either way. Kept the Train version of 11/09.
    - 4 were the pph4 FES reweighting, 'average_fes.py', 'launch_FES.sh',
      'FES_2D_inverse.py' and 'fes-rew.dat'. The LFER versions of 02/09 point at
      'rep_N/pph3-included' and widen the CV range to '--min=-1.5,-2.4', and they are
      the ones consistent with the 'pph3-included/' data and the 'fes-rew.dat' that
      actually sit there. Kept the LFER versions.
    - 'README': kept the Train version, 20449 bytes against 8662.
    - 'TS_barplot.py': kept the Train version, 533 lines against 171.
    - 'ts_levels.png': kept the LFER render of 17/09; both are in any case superseded
      by 'ts_levels_v3.png'.

o Only '__pycache__/TS_barplot.cpython-311.pyc' was deliberately dropped, being a
  regenerable bytecode cache.

o Verified before deleting anything, with job 46887868, a read-only
  'rsync -avhnc --itemize-changes' from the old tree into the merged one. It ran
  01:17:34 and reported exactly the six expected entries: the dropped '.pyc' and the
  five files where the LFER version was kept on purpose. Nine further files
  ('ts_energies.txt' and eight 'average_pmf_error.dat') showed a timestamp
  difference with no checksum difference, so identical content. Nothing else across
  947.78 GB. Only then was the old tree removed, which took 1m46s and brought the
  group's scratch use from 28.36 TB to 27.56 TB.

o 'Train_PPiMg2/LFER_3_mg2' now exists again, but as a SYMLINK to
  '../LFER/LFER_3_mg2'. It is a compatibility shim, not a copy, and it is there for a
  concrete reason: 159 scripts in the tree hardcode the absolute old path, nearly all
  of them to reach the NNP graphs -- 83 'convert_restart_to_lmp.py', 67
  'generate_US_window.py' and 7 'job-array_lammps-deepmd_explore_gpu_alogin1.sh'.
  Rather than edit 159 files, the old path was made to resolve again. Both spellings
  therefore reach the same data, and there is only one copy on disk.

o Because of that symlink, 'copy_LFER_3_mg2.sh' and 'verify_LFER_3_mg2.sh' became
  actively unsafe: their SRC would now resolve to the same directory as their DST, so
  the copy script would rsync the tree onto itself. Both are retired as
  '<name>.retired_20261002' and must not be run again.

o 'NNP_LFER_choice/' is deliberately NOT merged. Its two copies are byte-identical,
  12883 files each, so there is nothing to reconcile, but 121 GB of duplication
  remains in 'Train_PPiMg2/NNP_LFER_choice/' and 'LFER/NNP_LFER_choice/'. This is a
  conscious choice, not an oversight.

o The audit trail of the merge -- manifests, the per-file action log and the
  verification log -- is in '.merge_audit/' at this level.

